language Essence 1.3

$ A partial function may define no keys, some keys, or every key. Undefined keys do not
$ participate in the generator; an empty function therefore permits every bound.
find f : function int(1..2) --> int(10,20)
find bound : int(0..2)
find at_two : bool
such that
    and([i <= bound | i <- defined(f)]),
    at_two <-> (2 in defined(f)),
    !(0 in defined(f)),
    !(3 in defined(f))
